message: "If you use canli-fundamentals-mcp, please cite the software and its author."
title: "canli-fundamentals-mcp: SEC company fundamentals point in time, as an MCP server"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Canli"
    given-names: "Arhan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-4138-7907"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arhancanli/canli-fundamentals-mcp"
url: "https://canlicapital.com/developers#mcp-fundamentals"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - model context protocol
  - point-in-time data
  - SEC XBRL
  - restatements
  - lookahead bias
abstract: >-
  A Model Context Protocol server that answers, for any value a company reported to the SEC in
  XBRL, what was first reported, what the latest filing says and what was known on a given date,
  each with the filing behind it, so a backtest reads only what investors could have known. It
  computes locally from a hash-checked copy of the SEC companyfacts response and labels each
  later change as a stock split or a change of reporting tag where the filings show it.
